<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>Warriors Spirit
<p>

He walks without fear.  The very concept of fear is so alien to him that laughter often escapes him when most are speechless.  His purpose?  Well, A warriors purpose is protect and shield, using his own body to pay the bands Butcher’s Bill.   In matters of arms, he has the final say.  He is responsible for choosing the groups battles.  They must trust in him to choose.  He must trust in them for his health.  He is usually humble, this causes most to think him daft, however a good warrior must be canny, and reasonable.  Knowing his bands strengths and limitations, and working within them.   He is often unappreiciated,  most simply do not understand or see the way he operatates even though he makes no effort to hide.
<p>

Our band is currently camped on a ledge overlooking one of the most dangerous deserts on Norrath.  We are serving the good Gods by eliminating as many of the evil ones as we can.  The fact that there is a healthy profit involved is also part of our decision to fight here.  We must be careful though.  The area is heavily populated by evil races far superior in strength to us.    The magic users of our group tell me that their meditation is almost complete which tells me that its time to go to work.  I have been bored out of my mind while these caster types sat quietly meditating.   Hehe, I made arrows.    As my heartbeat quickens , I spring to my feet.  I know that its time for me to play my deadly game.  I will soon enter a dance with the devil, although I must find him first.  The sun is a furnace, and the sands shift, many a less hardy soul has perished just crossing this wasteland but I ignore the elements.  I am a true Warrior.  Cresting a dune I can discern several of the monsters hunting me even as I hunt them.   Choosing one, I mentally plan my retreat to my group’s camp, What route will take me there quickly but not near other monsters at the same time?  I know that we can defeat this beast, as long as he is alone.  I nock a arrow and let fly scoring a hit on the foul beast, and angering him greatly.  As he charges at me I laugh!  The Dance has begun.  Quickly I begin my run back to our campsite announcing that I am incomming and that it is time to party.  In the distance, I can see my group making ready.  As the distance between me and my band I begin to feel pain.  “Ouch!”  the Monster has caught up to me and is showing me just how angry he is…  HA!   Reaching the ledge I turn to the beast and draw my sword.  Now it is my turn to show my displeasure with him.  I don’t even realize how strong this monster is until I see the blue magic of our cleric’s healing surround me.  I thank her profusely and begin the dance anew!   Our Wizard types are now casting their spells with a vengence and the beast is bellowing in rage that we are hurting it….  He turns on the wizzard types to finish them.   “Oh Boy!   This won’t do! “  I know in my heart that although their magic is strong it is learned through the price of a weaker body.  Although my own health is halfway gone, I begin throwing curses at the beast.  Taunting him for all I am worth.  I smile as he turns back to me and let him hear again the song of my sword.  Again and again we dance to the deadly cadence of thunder created by our magic users until the beast is no more.  
&nbsp;</font></td></tr>

